<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spartocus I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 438–433 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Spartocus I was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spartocid-dynasty">Spartocid dynasty</a> of the Bosporan Kingdom, who took power at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panticapaeum">Panticapaeum</a> in 438 BCE after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archaeanactids">Archaeanactids</a> and ruled until 433 BCE, according to Diodorus. His name suggests a Thracian origin. His descendants ruled the Bosporus for more than three centuries.</p></div>
